.TH LIRIA 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
liria \- the SDE file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B liria
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIURI\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Liria browses and organizes the files and folders on your computer,
removable drives and the network. It has tabs, an extra pane, a Home overview
with quick access folders, drives and recent files, safe copying to USB drives
and extensions for archives (Taca) and terminals.
.PP
The window has one compact header row: Back, Forward and Parent Folder, the
path of the current folder, the view buttons (icons, list, compact), Search and
the main menu (F10). Press Ctrl+? for all keyboard shortcuts and F1 for help.
.PP
Liria does not manage the desktop: SDE keeps its own wallpaper and desktop icons.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-browser
Open a browser window.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tabs
Open the URIs in tabs of one window.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-default\-window
Only create windows for explicitly given URIs.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-select
Select the given URIs in their parent folders.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-geometry =\fIGEOMETRY\fR
Create the first window with the given geometry.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quit
Quit the running Liria.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the Liria version.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show all options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/liria/help/index.html
Liria help.
.TP
.I ~/.config/liria/
Bookmarks, accelerators and other user data.
